// result_begin: markdown
\image(figures/hierarchy_cell.svg)
// result_end

\caption(The residual cell combines an unchanged input with the gated projected branch. BN state belongs to three normalization layers and is checkpointed separately from weights.)
\alttext(Expansion, depthwise and projection stages feed squeeze/excitation and a residual output; separate project and identity routes enter the same output.)

BN uses population batch variance for normalization with epsilon.001, but unbiased batch
variance in the moving update. Momentum is.9. Training statistics and state mutation have
separate controls: training=true/update_stats=false supports gradient/inspection passes;
training=true/update_stats=true updates moving moments exactly once with the pre-update
forward. Inference uses detached moving means/variances. The caller excludes state from
Adam and saves/restores **both** stores. Missing buffers are lazily initialized, so restoring
weights alone silently gives different inference. Native tests demonstrate that difference.

Only two1×1 prior kernels are regularized. Each reshapes to a4×1 matrix, whose sole singular
value is its L2 norm. The source uses smoothed norms,
R=1e-4[sqrt(sum(W_pm²)+1e-12)+sqrt(sum(W_pl²)+1e-12)]. Train_loss=L+R; validation uses L.
This is not full NVAE's all-kernel spectral schedule or warmup. Isolated regularizer and
unregularized prior-head derivatives are saved before the first update.

> Native data and paired explicit fitting programs

Native beta-vae-assets preparation generates294 unique28×28 binary circle/square images:
shape2×size3×x7×y7, split deterministically into210 fit/42 validation/42 test. Source IDs are
disjoint; factors never enter either network or selection. The optional independent checker
regenerates all230,496 pixels and assignments. This teaching lattice is not a paper benchmark.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n                       = dm::nn;
  const std::filesystem::path cache = dm::datasets::data_home();
  dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("beta-vae-assets", cache.string());
  auto                       data = n::load_npz((cache / "beta_vae/factors.npz").string());
  std::set<int>              ids;
  std::set<std::vector<int>> images;
  for (auto& [name, value] : data) {
    if (name.ends_with("_images")) {
      for (int i = 0; i < value.size(0); ++i)
        if (!images.insert(n::select(value, 0, i).to_vector<int>()).second)
          return 1;
      value = n::cast(value, n::DType::Float32);
    }
    if (name.ends_with("_source_ids"))
      for (int id : value.to_vector<int>())
        if (!ids.insert(id).second)
          return 1;
  }
  if (ids.size() != 294 || images.size() != 294)
    return 1;
  for (const std::string variant : {"hierarchical", "miniature_nvae"}) {
    const auto root = std::filesystem::path("build/hierarchy") / variant;
    std::filesystem::create_directories(root);
    n::save_npz((root / "data.npz").string(), data);
    std::filesystem::copy_file(
        cache / "beta_vae/manifest.json",
        root / "data_manifest.json",
        std::filesystem::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
  }
  std::print("294 unique binary images and IDs; same210/42/42 pools for both architectures.\n");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
294 unique binary images and IDs; same210/42/42 pools for both architectures.
// result_end

Both fits use BatchOrder(210,32,2617), seven updates per epoch including a final18-row batch,
three epochs/21 updates each. Adam uses.003,.9/.999 and1e-8, on trainable weights only.
GaussianNoise supplies explicit51-coordinate banks: training seeds2664/2665/2666, fixed
four-draw fit2621/validation2633/test2647, prior2657. The local MT19937/Box–Muller Float64
values and Float32 casts are saved per variant. No forward draws noise internally.

Completed epochs1–3 compete on fixed four-draw **unregularized inference-mode** validation
negative ELBO. Lower KL is averaged over all top draws; every Float32 per-row term accumulates
in Float64, draw then row. The selected checkpoint contains weights and all moving buffers.
Extra first-gradient/forward/regularizer probes use batch moments without moving updates.
The actual training forward updates BN state once, then explicit gradients update only weights.
The complete program includes fresh restore, both-noise interventions, recursive greedy means,
fixed-noise repeatability, target-free decoding, single/batch parity, ancestral generation and
parameter/state immutability. Helpers contain only I/O, native forwards and metric aggregation.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <chrono>
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <fstream>
#include <iostream>
namespace nn = dm::nn;
void Require(bool condition, const std::string& why) {
  if (!condition)
    throw std::runtime_error(why);
}
void Near(double x, double y, double tolerance, const std::string& why) {
  Require(std::abs(x - y) <= tolerance, why);
}
struct BetaFactorData {
  nn::Tensor images, factors, source;
};
struct VaeNoiseBank {
  nn::Tensor standard, epsilon;
};
nn::Tensor Flatten(const nn::Tensor& t) {
  return nn::reshape(t, {t.size(0), 784});
}
nn::Tensor Find(const nn::NamedTensors& a, const std::string& key) {
  for (const auto& [k, v] : a)
    if (k == key)
      return v;
  throw std::runtime_error(key);
}
std::vector<float> Bytes(const nn::Tensor& t) {
  return t.contiguous().to_vector<float>();
}
nn::NamedTensors Arrays(const nn::ParameterStore& p) {
  nn::NamedTensors a;
  for (const auto& k : p.names())
    a.emplace_back(k, p.at(k).detach().clone());
  return a;
}
auto Snapshot(const nn::ParameterStore& p) {
  return p.flatten();
}
nn::NamedTensors CheckGradients(
    const nn::ParameterStore&      p,
    const std::vector<nn::Tensor>& gs,
    const std::string&,
    const std::string&) {
  nn::NamedTensors a;
  Require(gs.size() == p.size(), "all10 gradients");
  const auto names = p.names();
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < gs.size(); ++i) {
    double norm = 0;
    for (double x : gs[i].to_vector<double>()) {
      Require(std::isfinite(x), "finite derivatives");
      norm += x * x;
    }
    Require(norm > 0, "nonzero derivative in each tensor");
    a.emplace_back(names[i], gs[i]);
  }
  return a;
}

VaeNoiseBank HierarchyNoise(std::int64_t n, std::int64_t samples, std::uint32_t seed) {
  const auto standard = nn::models::GaussianNoise({n, 51}, samples, seed);
  return {standard, nn::cast(standard, nn::DType::Float32)};
}
nn::Tensor HierarchyNoiseAt(const VaeNoiseBank& bank, int k) {
  Require(k >= 0 && k < bank.epsilon.size(0), "available hierarchy draw");
  return nn::select(bank.epsilon, 0, k).contiguous();
}
nn::NamedTensors Arrays(const nn::ParameterStore& p, const nn::ParameterStore& state) {
  auto out = Arrays(p);
  for (const auto& name : state.names())
    out.emplace_back("state/" + name, state.at(name).detach().clone());
  return out;
}
auto Snapshot(const nn::ParameterStore& p, const nn::ParameterStore& state) {
  std::vector<std::vector<float>> out;
  for (const auto& [name, t] : Arrays(p, state))
    out.push_back(Bytes(t));
  return out;
}
void Load(nn::ParameterStore& p, nn::ParameterStore& state, const std::string& file) {
  auto arrays = nn::load_npz(file);
  Require(arrays.size() == p.size() + state.size(), "all weights and statistics");
  for (const auto& [name, value] : arrays) {
    const bool stat  = name.starts_with("state/");
    auto&      store = stat ? state : p;
    const auto key   = stat ? name.substr(6) : name;
    Require(store.contains(key) && store.at(key).shape() == value.shape(), "matching checkpoint");
    store.set(key, value.contiguous().clone());
  }
}
nn::NamedTensors Evaluate(
    nn::ParameterStore& p,
    nn::ParameterStore& state,
    bool                nvae,
    const nn::Tensor&   images,
    const nn::Tensor&   noise,
    bool                training = false) {
  nn::NoGradGuard guard;
  const auto      o = nn::models::HierarchicalVariationalAutoencoder(
      p, state, Flatten(images), noise, nvae, training, false);
  nn::NamedTensors out{
      {"encoder_feature", o.encoder_feature},
      {"top_feature", o.top_feature},
      {"top_mu", o.top_mu},
      {"top_lv", o.top_lv},
      {"top_z", o.top_z},
      {"prior_mu", o.prior_mu},
      {"prior_lv", o.prior_lv},
      {"head_mu", o.head_mu},
      {"head_lv", o.head_lv},
      {"lower_mu", o.lower_mu},
      {"lower_lv", o.lower_lv},
      {"lower_z", o.lower_z},
      {"probability", o.probability},
      {"nll", o.nll},
      {"kl_lower", o.kl_lower},
      {"kl_top", o.kl_top},
      {"loss", o.loss},
      {"regularizer", o.regularizer},
      {"train_loss", o.train_loss}};
  for (auto& [name, t] : out) {
    t = t.contiguous();
    for (double v : t.to_vector<double>())
      Require(std::isfinite(v), "finite hierarchy fields");
  }
  return out;
}
nn::Tensor Decode(
    nn::ParameterStore& p,
    nn::ParameterStore& state,
    bool                nvae,
    const nn::Tensor&   lower,
    const nn::Tensor&   top) {
  nn::NoGradGuard guard;
  return nn::models::HierarchyDecode(p, state, lower, top, nvae).contiguous();
}
nn::NamedTensors Prior(
    nn::ParameterStore& p,
    nn::ParameterStore& state,
    bool                nvae,
    const nn::Tensor&   top,
    const nn::Tensor&   lower_noise) {
  nn::NoGradGuard guard;
  const auto      o = nn::models::HierarchyPrior(p, state, top, lower_noise, nvae);
  return {
      {"top_z", o.top_z},
      {"lower_noise", o.lower_noise},
      {"prior_mu", o.prior_mu.contiguous()},
      {"prior_lv", o.prior_lv.contiguous()},
      {"lower_z", o.lower_z.contiguous()},
      {"probability", o.probability.contiguous()}};
}
std::vector<double> HierarchyScore(
    nn::ParameterStore& p,
    nn::ParameterStore& state,
    bool                nvae,
    const nn::Tensor&   images,
    const VaeNoiseBank& bank) {
  double     nll = 0, lower = 0, top = 0;
  const auto n = images.size(0), samples = bank.epsilon.size(0);
  for (int k = 0; k < samples; ++k) {
    auto f = Evaluate(p, state, nvae, images, HierarchyNoiseAt(bank, k));
    auto a = Find(f, "nll").to_vector<float>(), b = Find(f, "kl_lower").to_vector<float>(),
         c = Find(f, "kl_top").to_vector<float>();
    for (int row = 0; row < n; ++row) {
      nll += a[row];
      lower += b[row];
      top += c[row];
    }
  }
  const double count = double(n * samples);
  return {nll / count, lower / count, top / count, (nll + lower + top) / count};
}
double MaxAbsDiff(const nn::Tensor& a, const nn::Tensor& b, int n) {
  const auto x = Bytes(a), y = Bytes(b);
  double     d = 0;
  for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i)
    d = std::max(d, std::abs(double(x[i]) - y[i]));
  return d;
}
double Mse(const nn::Tensor& a, const nn::Tensor& b) {
  return nn::mean(
             nn::square(
                 nn::cast(Flatten(a), nn::DType::Float64) -
                 nn::cast(Flatten(b), nn::DType::Float64)))
      .item();
}

double Difference(const nn::Tensor& a, const nn::Tensor& b) {
  Require(a.shape() == b.shape(), "matching shapes");
  return MaxAbsDiff(a, b, int(a.numel()));
}
nn::Tensor PixelMean(const nn::Tensor& images) {
  const auto         v = Flatten(images).to_vector<float>();
  std::vector<float> mean(784);
  for (int j = 0; j < 784; ++j) {
    double total = 0;
    for (int b = 0; b < images.size(0); ++b)
      total += v[b * 784 + j];
    mean[j] = float(total / double(images.size(0)));
  }
  return nn::from_vector(mean, {784});
}
nn::Tensor Constant(const nn::Tensor& row, int count) {
  return nn::broadcast_to(nn::reshape(row, {1, 784}), {count, 784}).contiguous();
}
void Checks(const std::filesystem::path& root) {
  auto pm = nn::tensor({{1.f, -2.f, .5f}}), pl = nn::tensor({{.2f, -.4f, .6f}}),
       zero = nn::zeros({1, 3});
  auto q    = nn::models::HierarchyPosterior(pm, pl, zero, zero, true);
  auto kl   = nn::models::ConditionalGaussianKl(q.mu, q.log_variance, pm, pl);
  Near(kl.to_vector<float>()[0], 0, 0, "NVAE zero-residual KL exactly zero");
  nn::save_npz(
      (root / "residual_algebra.npz").string(),
      {{"prior_mu", q.mu}, {"prior_lv", q.log_variance}, {"kl", kl}});
  std::cout << "residual posterior zero correction gives prior/KL0 passed" << std::endl;
}

double Train(const std::filesystem::path& root, int epochs, bool nvae) {
  const auto                  data = nn::load_npz((root / "data.npz").string());
  std::vector<BetaFactorData> pools;
  for (const std::string split : {"fit", "validation", "test"})
    pools.push_back(
        {Find(data, split + "_images"),
         Find(data, split + "_factors"),
         Find(data, split + "_source_ids")});
  std::filesystem::create_directories(root);
  Checks(root);
  std::vector<VaeNoiseBank> noise{
      HierarchyNoise(210, 4, 2621), HierarchyNoise(42, 4, 2633), HierarchyNoise(42, 4, 2647)},
      training;
  auto             prior_noise = HierarchyNoise(20, 1, 2657);
  nn::NamedTensors fixed{
      {"prior_standard", prior_noise.standard}, {"prior_epsilon", prior_noise.epsilon}};
  for (int split = 0; split < 3; ++split) {
    const std::string name = split == 0 ? "fit" : split == 1 ? "validation" : "test";
    fixed.emplace_back(name + "_standard", noise[split].standard);
    fixed.emplace_back(name + "_epsilon", noise[split].epsilon);
  }
  nn::save_npz((root / "fixed_noise.npz").string(), fixed);
  for (int e = 1; e <= epochs; ++e) {
    training.push_back(HierarchyNoise(210, 1, 2663 + e));
    nn::save_npz(
        (root / ("train_noise_epoch" + std::to_string(e) + ".npz")).string(),
        {{"standard", training.back().standard}, {"epsilon", training.back().epsilon}});
  }
  nn::ParameterStore model(2609), state(0);
  {
    nn::NoGradGuard guard;
    nn::models::HierarchicalVariationalAutoencoder(
        model, state, nn::zeros({2, 784}), nn::zeros({2, 51}), nvae);
  }
  nn::OptimizerConfig config;
  config.kind = nn::OptimizerKind::Adam;
  nn::Optimizer optimizer(model, .003, config);
  Require(
      model.size() == (nvae ? 37u : 26u) && model.count() == (nvae ? 2027 : 1977) &&
          state.size() == (nvae ? 6u : 0u),
      "spatial hierarchy/NVAE parameter and BN census");
  nn::save_npz((root / "initial_arrays.npz").string(), Arrays(model, state));
  nn::BatchOrder order(210, 32, 2617);
  std::ofstream  history(root / "history.tsv"), batches(root / "batches.tsv");
  history.precision(17);
  history << "epoch\ttrain_preupdate_negative_elbo\tvalidation_nll\tvalidation_lower_"
             "kl\tvalidation_top_kl\t"
             "validation_negative_elbo\n";
  batches << "epoch\tstep\trow\tsource_id\n";
  const auto fit_source = pools[0].source.to_vector<int>();
  const auto best_path  = (root / "best.npz").string();
  double     best       = std::numeric_limits<double>::infinity();
  int        selected = 0, step = 0;
  const auto started = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
  for (int epoch = 1; epoch <= epochs; ++epoch) {
    order.begin_epoch();
    double sum     = 0;
    int    seen    = 0;
    auto   epsilon = HierarchyNoiseAt(training[epoch - 1], 0);
    for (;;) {
      auto rows = order.next();
      if (rows.empty())
        break;
      auto x = nn::take_rows(pools[0].images, rows), e = nn::take_rows(epsilon, rows);
      if (step == 0) {
        nn::save_npz((root / "first_batch.npz").string(), {{"images", x}, {"epsilon", e}});
        auto g = CheckGradients(
            model,
            nn::grad(
                nn::models::HierarchicalVariationalAutoencoder(
                    model, state, Flatten(x), e, nvae, true, false)
                    .train_loss,
                model.parameters()),
            "all hierarchy gradients finite",
            "all hierarchy/NVAE trainable tensors receive gradients");
        nn::save_npz((root / "first_gradients.npz").string(), g);
        nn::save_npz(
            (root / "first_forward.npz").string(), Evaluate(model, state, nvae, x, e, true));
        if (nvae) {
          const auto o = nn::models::HierarchicalVariationalAutoencoder(
              model, state, Flatten(x), e, true, true, false);
          const std::vector<nn::Tensor> heads{model.at("prior_mu/W"), model.at("prior_lv/W")};
          nn::GradOptions               keep;
          keep.retain_graph = true;
          const auto r = nn::grad(o.regularizer, heads, keep), l = nn::grad(o.loss, heads);
          nn::save_npz(
              (root / "first_regularizer_gradients.npz").string(),
              {{"regularizer/prior_mu/W", r[0]},
               {"regularizer/prior_lv/W", r[1]},
               {"without_regularizer/prior_mu/W", l[0]},
               {"without_regularizer/prior_lv/W", l[1]}});
        }
      }
      const auto out = nn::models::HierarchicalVariationalAutoencoder(
          model, state, Flatten(x), e, nvae, true, true);
      sum += double(rows.size()) * out.train_loss.item<float>();
      const auto gradients = nn::grad(out.train_loss, model.parameters());
      optimizer.step(gradients);
      seen += int(rows.size());
      for (auto row : rows)
        batches << epoch << '\t' << step << '\t' << row << '\t' << fit_source[row] << '\n';
      if (step == 0)
        nn::save_npz((root / "first_update_arrays.npz").string(), Arrays(model, state));
      ++step;
    }
    Require(seen == 210, "all210fitting cases once per epoch");
    auto score = HierarchyScore(model, state, nvae, pools[1].images, noise[1]);
    history << epoch << '\t' << sum / seen;
    for (auto value : score)
      history << '\t' << value;
    history << '\n';
    nn::save_npz(
        (root / ("epoch" + std::to_string(epoch) + "_arrays.npz")).string(), Arrays(model, state));
    if (score[3] < best) {
      best     = score[3];
      selected = epoch;
      nn::save_npz(
          best_path,
          Arrays(
              model,
              state)); // four-sample validation ELBO selects checkpoint (weights + BN statistics)
    }
    std::cout << "epoch" << epoch << ":validation NLL=" << score[0] << ",lowerKL=" << score[1]
              << ",topKL=" << score[2] << ",negativeELBO=" << score[3] << std::endl;
  }
  const double seconds =
      std::chrono::duration<double>(std::chrono::steady_clock::now() - started).count();
  nn::ParameterStore deployed(2609), deployed_state(0);
  {
    nn::NoGradGuard guard;
    nn::models::HierarchicalVariationalAutoencoder(
        deployed, deployed_state, nn::zeros({2, 784}), nn::zeros({2, 51}), nvae);
  }
  Load(deployed, deployed_state, best_path);
  Near(
      HierarchyScore(deployed, deployed_state, nvae, pools[1].images, noise[1])[3],
      best,
      1e-8,
      "fresh selected validation score");
  const auto       before = Snapshot(deployed, deployed_state);
  nn::NamedTensors output;
  for (int split = 0; split < 3; ++split) {
    const std::int64_t n    = pools[split].images.size(0);
    const std::string  name = split == 0 ? "fit" : split == 1 ? "validation" : "test";
    auto greedy = Evaluate(deployed, deployed_state, nvae, pools[split].images, nn::zeros({n, 51}));
    Require(
        Bytes(Find(greedy, "lower_z")) == Bytes(Find(greedy, "lower_mu")) &&
            Bytes(Find(greedy, "top_z")) == Bytes(Find(greedy, "top_mu")),
        "both zero-noise samples equal their recursive means");
    for (const auto& [key, value] : greedy)
      output.emplace_back(name + "_greedy_" + key, value);
    for (int k = 0; k < 4; ++k) {
      auto f = Evaluate(
          deployed, deployed_state, nvae, pools[split].images, HierarchyNoiseAt(noise[split], k));
      for (const auto& [key, value] : f)
        output.emplace_back(name + "_draw" + std::to_string(k) + "_" + key, value);
    }
  }
  auto test =
           Evaluate(deployed, deployed_state, nvae, pools[2].images, HierarchyNoiseAt(noise[2], 0)),
       repeat =
           Evaluate(deployed, deployed_state, nvae, pools[2].images, HierarchyNoiseAt(noise[2], 0));
  Require(
      Bytes(Find(test, "probability")) == Bytes(Find(repeat, "probability")) &&
          Bytes(Find(test, "probability")) ==
              Bytes(Decode(
                  deployed, deployed_state, nvae, Find(test, "lower_z"), Find(test, "top_z"))),
      "repeat and target-free lower latent decode BITEXACT");
  auto single = Evaluate(
      deployed,
      deployed_state,
      nvae,
      nn::take_rows(pools[2].images, {0}),
      nn::take_rows(HierarchyNoiseAt(noise[2], 0), {0}));
  const double parity = MaxAbsDiff(Find(single, "probability"), Find(test, "probability"), 784);
  Require(parity < 2e-6, "single/batch parity");
  std::vector<float> lower_v(42 * 51, 0.f), top_v(42 * 51, 0.f);
  for (int b = 0; b < 42; ++b) {
    for (int j = 0; j < 49; ++j)
      lower_v[b * 51 + j] = .5f;
    for (int j = 49; j < 51; ++j)
      top_v[b * 51 + j] = .5f;
  }
  auto base = Evaluate(deployed, deployed_state, nvae, pools[2].images, nn::zeros({42, 51})),
       low  = Evaluate(
           deployed, deployed_state, nvae, pools[2].images, nn::from_vector(lower_v, {42, 51})),
       top = Evaluate(
           deployed, deployed_state, nvae, pools[2].images, nn::from_vector(top_v, {42, 51}));
  Require(
      Bytes(Find(base, "lower_mu")) == Bytes(Find(low, "lower_mu")) &&
          Bytes(Find(base, "prior_mu")) == Bytes(Find(low, "prior_mu")) &&
          Difference(Find(base, "lower_z"), Find(low, "lower_z")) > 1e-4,
      "lower noise changes sample only,not hierarchy heads");
  const double prior_effect  = Difference(Find(base, "prior_mu"), Find(top, "prior_mu")),
               fusion_effect = Difference(Find(base, "lower_mu"), Find(top, "lower_mu"));
  Require(
      prior_effect > 1e-5 && fusion_effect > 1e-5,
      "top noise changes conditional prior AND conditional lower posterior");
  nn::save_npz((root / "top_noise_intervention.npz").string(), top);
  nn::save_npz((root / "lower_noise_intervention.npz").string(), low);
  auto prior_bank = HierarchyNoiseAt(prior_noise, 0);
  auto e1         = nn::slice_axis(prior_bank, 1, 0, 49).contiguous(),
       z2         = nn::slice_axis(prior_bank, 1, 49, 51).contiguous();
  auto prior      = Prior(deployed, deployed_state, nvae, z2, e1);
  Require(
      Bytes(Find(prior, "probability")) ==
          Bytes(
              Decode(deployed, deployed_state, nvae, Find(prior, "lower_z"), Find(prior, "top_z"))),
      "ancestral hierarchical sample decodes exactly");
  nn::save_npz((root / "prior.npz").string(), prior);
  Require(
      before == Snapshot(deployed, deployed_state),
      "all inference/prior/intervention calls immutable");
  nn::save_npz((root / "outputs.npz").string(), output);
  nn::save_npz((root / "model_arrays.npz").string(), Arrays(deployed, deployed_state));
  auto          score = HierarchyScore(deployed, deployed_state, nvae, pools[2].images, noise[2]);
  const double  mse   = Mse(Find(output, "test_greedy_probability"), pools[2].images);
  auto          mean  = Constant(PixelMean(pools[0].images), 42);
  const double  mean_mse = Mse(mean, pools[2].images);
  std::ofstream meta(root / "metrics.json");
  meta.precision(17);
  meta << "{\"miniature_nvae\":" << (nvae ? "true" : "false") << ",\"parameters\":" << model.count()
       << ",\"tensors\":" << model.size() << ",\"state_tensors\":" << state.size()
       << ",\"epochs\":" << epochs << ",\"updates\":" << step << ",\"selected_epoch\":" << selected
       << ",\"mc_samples\":4,\"test_nll\":" << score[0] << ",\"test_lower_kl\":" << score[1]
       << ",\"test_top_kl\":" << score[2] << ",\"test_negative_elbo\":" << score[3]
       << ",\"greedy_decode_test_mse\":" << mse << ",\"fit_mean_test_mse\":" << mean_mse
       << ",\"single_batch_max_error\":" << parity
       << ",\"top_noise_prior_mu_max_effect\":" << prior_effect
       << ",\"top_noise_posterior_mu_max_effect\":" << fusion_effect
       << ",\"training_seconds\":" << seconds << "}\n";

  std::print(
      "| {} | {} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} |\n",
      nvae ? "miniature NVAE" : "hierarchy",
      selected,
      score[0],
      score[1],
      score[2],
      score[3],
      mse,
      mean_mse);
  return seconds;
}
int main() {
  std::print(
      "| model | selected epoch | test NLL | lower KL | top KL | negative ELBO | greedy MSE | fit "
      "mean MSE |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n");
  Train("build/hierarchy/hierarchical", 3, false);
  Train("build/hierarchy/miniature_nvae", 3, true);
}
```
