> Selected results and limitations of recursive greedy means

Both select epoch3. Ordinary hierarchy test NLL237.742755, lower KL1.343193 and top KL0.481632
give negative ELBO239.567580. Miniature NVAE gives292.300600+2.304885+2.958491=297.563977
nats/image. Different architectures and parameter/state counts prevent a controlled quality
comparison. Greedy reconstructions set both epsilons to zero recursively; they are not posterior
predictive means. MSE0.104085294/0.106240368 is worse than fitting-only mean0.048548290.
Three short epochs do not establish useful semantic hierarchy, superior inference or generation.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/hierarchy_learning.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  auto chart = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  for (const std::string model : {"hierarchical", "miniature_nvae"}) {
    std::ifstream f("build/hierarchy/" + model + "/history.tsv");
    std::string   line;
    std::getline(f, line);
    std::vector<double> epoch, criterion;
    while (std::getline(f, line)) {
      std::istringstream row(line);
      double             e, train, nll, lower, top, total;
      row >> e >> train >> nll >> lower >> top >> total;
      epoch.push_back(e);
      criterion.push_back(total);
    }
    chart.lines(
        epoch,
        criterion,
        model,
        model == "hierarchical" ? dm::RGBA{37, 99, 235} : dm::RGBA{220, 38, 38},
        2);
  }
  chart.title("Fixed four-draw inference-mode validation")
      .x_label("completed epoch")
      .y_label("unregularized negative ELBO / nats per image")
      .save_svg("build/hierarchy_learning.svg");
}
